  "body": "## What changed\n\nAI Chat classifies cloud provider authentication failures and displays a safe key rejected status.\n\n- Classify provider authentication failures (`is_auth_failure`) across all cloud providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini).\n- Handle Google Gemini authentication failure responses (HTTP 400 with `API_KEY_INVALID` or `API key not valid`, and HTTP 403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`) as key rejected instead of a generic model error.\n- Guard against echoed model names: model names are never treated as authentication evidence, and explicit model refusals remain distinct.\n- Keep non-authentication failures (HTTP 404 model not found, HTTP 402 billing, HTTP 429 rate limit, HTTP 500 server unavailable, and network unreachable) distinct from authentication failures.\n- Redact secrets so that raw secret keys and unredacted provider payloads are never exposed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore: Gemini HTTP 400 displays that the provider refused the request or the model name.\n\n![Before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSwetz/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3845/before.png)\n\nAfter: Gemini HTTP 400 displays that the provider rejected the key and advises setting a new key.\n\n![After](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JSwetz/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3845/after.png)\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `anthropic_cloud_test_authentication_failure_shows_key_rejected`: loopback test pins that Anthropic HTTP 401 shows key rejected and redacts secrets.\n- `gemini_cloud_test_bad_request_auth_failure_shows_key_rejected`: loopback test pins that Gemini HTTP 400 `API_KEY_INVALID` shows key rejected.\n- `gemini_cloud_test_forbidden_auth_failure_shows_key_rejected`: loopback test pins that Gemini HTTP 403 `PERMISSION_DENIED` shows key rejected.\n- `failed_cloud_test_shows_provider_type_code_and_endpoint`: loopback test pins OpenAI HTTP 401 key rejected.\n- `non_auth_cloud_test_failures_remain_distinct_from_key_rejected`: loopback test pins that HTTP 404 does not show key rejected.\n- `failed_test_names_the_cause_the_model_and_what_to_try`: unit tests verify provider status mapping table.\n- `bad_request_model_is_not_authentication_evidence`: pins that echoed model names across accepted tokens remain model refusals and not key rejections.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Real remote cloud provider networks (loopback mock servers used for deterministic testing).\n\nChangelog: AI Chat shows a key rejected status when a cloud provider rejects an API key.\n\nFixes #3804\n",
